      "title": "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "16d4b83c-29c5-52cb-baea-0e9ec357ad53",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-15 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-17\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} &=-32 \\\\ {x}_{1} &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-4$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-17 \\\\ 4(-4)+{x}_{2} &=-17 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-4$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ (-4)+2(-1) &=-5 \\\\ -6 &=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement.\n\nSo, the system has no solution.",
