    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0aa10b55-2c1f-5298-b961-4b7854ca495f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} &=-16 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=8$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ {x}_{1}-(8) &=-9 \\\\ {x}_{1} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=8$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=21 \\\\ 2(-1)+3(8) &=21 \\\\ 22 &=21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement.\n\nSo, the system has no solution.",
