  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119807,
      "id": "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2",
      "title": "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "66e64ccd-34d7-5a38-90e0-423406db4ad9",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} &=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ {x}_{1}-(2) &=-6 \\\\ {x}_{1} &=-4 \\\\ {x}_{1} &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-4$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ 2(-4)+3(2) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement.\n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-4$ and ${x}_{2}=2$, which means\n\n$$\n-4{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-4)+(2)=-2.\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b4bed8be-4a69-596c-bd78-5b6e912cbf17",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
